{% if render_mode == "stable" or render_mode == "thoughts" or render_mode == "transform" or (render_mode == "full" and not default(stable_split, false)) %}
{# One NPC attending another in their work hours, from both sides, with the role the player gave it in their own words (sever_attending,
   sever_attended_by: JSON, "" for none). Ships with the DLL that registers them. A retainer's post itself is 0168's. #}
{% if actorUUID and actorUUID != 0 %}
{% set saAttending = sever_attending(actorUUID) %}
{% if isObject(saAttending) %}
## Whom You Attend
{% if saAttending.retainer %}
- At your post with {{ saAttending.principal }}, your role is: {{ saAttending.role }}
{% else %}
{% if saAttending.captive %}
- {% if saAttending.allDay %}At all hours{% else %}In your working hours{% endif %} you keep watch over {{ saAttending.principal }}, who is held captive. Your task is to keep them held and stop an escape, not to set them free.
{% else %}
- {% if saAttending.allDay %}At all hours{% else %}In your working hours{% endif %} you attend {{ saAttending.principal }}: you keep close to them, see to them and defend them if they are attacked.
{% endif %}
{% if saAttending.role != "" %}
- Your role with them: {{ saAttending.role }}
{% endif %}
- This is an established part of your life. What it means between the two of you follows from the role and from who you are.
{% endif %}
{% if is_sever_follower(actorUUID) == "true" %}
- While you travel with {{ player.name }}, this post waits; you go back to it when the two of you part.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% set saAttendedBy = sever_attended_by(actorUUID) %}
{% if isObject(saAttendedBy) %}
## Who {% if saAttendedBy.captive %}Guards{% else %}Attends{% endif %} You
{% for a in saAttendedBy.attendants %}
- {{ a.name }}{% if a.role != "" %} (role: {{ a.role }}){% endif %}, {% if a.allDay %}at all hours{% else %}in their working hours{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if saAttendedBy.more > 0 %}
- {{ saAttendedBy.more }} more besides
{% endif %}
{% if saAttendedBy.captive %}
- They are there to keep you held.
{% else %}
- They keep close to you, see to you and defend you if you are attacked. This is an established part of your life; treat each of them as their role suggests.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}